From c65c81954c0cf59a2fe7594b709d3bd8a1c04058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:42:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0341 -- WaveBlaster MIDI through the
 RTC-paced replay

0207 plans MIDI ahead and replays it from the SB IRQ, but WaveBlaster
never got it. The default MPU transport paces every byte with a 320 us
busy-wait, the DreamBlaster input-overrun fix. SDL 0193 only replays
the blind transport. So WB fell back to the main-loop poll and played
in clumps at the render rate: SB5W had 69% of events more than 50 ms
late at the 6 fps intro.

SDL 0260 adds queue kind 3. The SB IRQ releases a slot's bytes and the
CMOS RTC periodic interrupt writes them, one per tick, at the
transport's spacing. When kind 2 is refused for a WaveBlaster, the
player now asks for kind 3. The plan, stamps, pause, stop and
song-change handling stay the same. Anything that refuses both kinds,
including the SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_WB_RTC_PUMP=0 killswitch, keeps the
poll.

The status line reports midi_tick=rtc, with the pump's rate, byte gap,
RTC ticks, the BIOS waits it serviced, and the longest
release-to-write. It also adds clk_uc=, song ms over uclock ms since
the first plan. That is a second view of the song clock beside the
CMOS-based clk=. It shares 0208's uclock calibration, so it mostly
checks that arithmetic; clk= is the independent witness. The status
buffers grow to fit (MIDI fragment 320 -> 512, status 512 -> 768), so
the line is not cut off the way 0207's once was.

